description:
# A1 - Fix connectWebSocket(): dispose stale/half-open sockets so reconnect runs

Primary file: `src/background/index.ts` (`connectWebSocket`, ~734-768)
Related: `src/app/ws/client.ts` (`isConnected`/`isConnectionHealthy`), `tests/app/ws-client.test.ts`, `tests/background/*`

## Problem (verified root cause of "won't wake")
After OS resume, a suspended TCP socket is commonly **half-open**: `readyState === OPEN` but the connection is dead and `onclose` may never fire. `connectWebSocket()` early-returns on `isConnected()` (OPEN) and therefore never disposes/recreates the zombie. `reconcileWake` keeps transitioning to `RECONNECTING` (icon "connecting") while `connectWebSocket()` no-ops — a permanent stall until manual Force Wake.

## Evidence
```ts
// src/background/index.ts:734
function connectWebSocket(): void {
  if (websocketClient) {
    const isConnected = websocketClient.isConnected();                 // readyState === OPEN
    const isConnecting = websocketClient.getReadyState() === WebSocket.CONNECTING;
    if (isConnected || isConnecting) { /* "skipping duplicate" */ return; }  // <-- STALL
  }
  // unreachable for a half-open socket:
  if (websocketClient) { websocketClient.disconnect(); websocketClient = null; }
  websocketClient = new WebSocketClient(WEBSOCKET_URL, getApiKey);
  setWebSocketClient(websocketClient);
  websocketClient.connect();
}
```
```ts
// src/app/ws/client.ts:64
isConnected(): boolean { return this.socket !== null && this.socket.readyState === WS_READY_STATE.OPEN; }
// src/app/ws/client.ts:363
public isConnectionHealthy(): boolean {
  if (this.socket?.readyState !== WS_READY_STATE.OPEN) return false;
  const age = Date.now() - this.lastNopAt;
  return age >= 0 && age <= 60000; // recent nop seen
}
```

## Fix
Treat "connected but unhealthy" (stale nop) as needing replacement, and dispose before recreating:
```ts
function connectWebSocket(): void {
  if (websocketClient) {
    const live = websocketClient.isConnected() && websocketClient.isConnectionHealthy();
    const isConnecting = websocketClient.getReadyState() === WebSocket.CONNECTING;
    if (live || isConnecting) {
      debugLogger.websocket("DEBUG", "WebSocket live or connecting, skipping duplicate connect");
      return;
    }
    // OPEN-but-stale (half-open after resume), CLOSING, or CLOSED -> dispose and rebuild
    debugLogger.websocket("INFO", "Disposing stale/unhealthy socket before reconnect", {
      readyState: websocketClient.getReadyState(),
    });
    websocketClient.disconnect();
    websocketClient = null;
  }
  websocketClient = new WebSocketClient(WEBSOCKET_URL, getApiKey);
  setWebSocketClient(websocketClient);
  websocketClient.connect();
}
```
Optional hardening: record a connect-attempt timestamp so a socket stuck in CONNECTING after resume is also replaced after N seconds.

## Acceptance criteria
- With `isConnected()===true` but `isConnectionHealthy()===false`, `connectWebSocket()` disposes the old socket and creates a new one.
- With a genuinely healthy socket, `connectWebSocket()` still no-ops.
- A test simulates the post-hibernate half-open case (OPEN + `lastNopAt` far in the past).

## Verification
`npx vitest run tests/app/ws-client.test.ts tests/background`; `npm run typecheck`; `npm run lint` on touched files.

## Scope / parallelization
Self-contained logic change in `connectWebSocket`. Blocks A4. Ignore version bump (done once at the end).

## File Scope
Primary file: `src/debug-dashboard/index.ts`

## Problem
The debug dashboard inserts log messages, JSON data, error messages, stacks, config, and system info through `innerHTML`. These values can originate from Pushbullet payloads, API errors, WebSocket close reasons, or exception messages.

## Evidence
```ts
// src/debug-dashboard/index.ts
logsContainer.innerHTML = [...filteredLogs].reverse().map(log => {
  const dataStr = log.data ? JSON.stringify(log.data, null, 2) : '';
  const errorStr = log.error ? `${log.error.name}: ${log.error.message}` : '';

  return `
    <div class="log-entry ${log.level}">
      <div class="log-message">${log.message}</div>
      ${dataStr ? `<div class="log-data">${dataStr}</div>` : ''}
      ${errorStr ? `<div class="log-data error">${errorStr}</div>` : ''}
    </div>
  `;
}).join('');
```

## Mitigation
Use DOM construction and `textContent` for dynamic values.

```ts
const entry = document.createElement('div');
entry.className = `log-entry ${safeLogLevel(log.level)}`;

const message = document.createElement('div');
message.className = 'log-message';
message.textContent = log.message;
entry.appendChild(message);

if (log.data) {
  const pre = document.createElement('pre');
  pre.className = 'log-data';
  pre.textContent = JSON.stringify(log.data, null, 2);
  entry.appendChild(pre);
}

logsContainer.replaceChildren(entry);
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- Log message/data/error rendering does not use string templates assigned to `innerHTML`.
- Critical error rendering does not interpolate error name, message, category, timestamp, or stack into HTML strings.
- Config/system JSON is rendered through `textContent` on `pre` nodes.
- Tests prove hostile HTML appears as text and does not create DOM elements.

## File Scope
Primary files:
- `src/lib/logging/index.ts`
- `src/background/index.ts`
- `src/background/utils.ts`
- `src/app/api/client.ts`
- `src/popup/index.ts`

## Problem
Debug logging captures complete decrypted pushes, SMS/file push objects, raw devices, and outbound push data. The sanitizer only redacts keys containing `token`, `key`, or `password`.

## Evidence
```ts
// src/background/index.ts
debugLogger.general("DEBUG", "FULL DECRYPTED PUSH DATA", {
  completeData: decryptedPush,
});
```

```ts
// src/background/utils.ts
debugLogger.notifications("DEBUG", "Complete sms_changed push object received", { push });
debugLogger.notifications("DEBUG", "Complete file push object received", { push });
```

```ts
// src/app/api/client.ts
debugLogger.general('INFO', `[DEVICE_DEBUG] Device #${index + 1}`, {
  pushToken: device.push_token ? `${device.push_token.substring(0, 8)}...` : '(no push token)',
  rawDevice: device,
});
```

## Mitigation
Replace full-object logs with summaries:

```ts
function summarizePush(push: Push): Record<string, unknown> {
  return {
    iden: push.iden,
    type: push.type,
    encrypted: !!push.encrypted,
    hasTitle: typeof push.title === 'string' && push.title.length > 0,
    hasBody: typeof push.body === 'string' && push.body.length > 0,
    hasUrl: typeof push.url === 'string' && push.url.length > 0,
    created: push.created,
    modified: push.modified,
  };
}
```

Expand redaction:

```ts
const SENSITIVE_KEYS = /token|key|password|secret|body|title|url|file_url|image_url|email|phone|address/i;

if (SENSITIVE_KEYS.test(key)) {
  sanitized[key] = '[redacted]';
} else {
  sanitized[key] = sanitize(value);
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- `rg "FULL DECRYPTED|Complete sms_changed|Complete file push|rawDevice|pushData" src` has no sensitive full-payload logging sites.
- Exported logs redact `body`, `title`, `url`, `file_url`, `image_url`, `email`, phone-like fields, API keys, tokens, and passwords.
- Tests cover nested object redaction and arrays.

## Purpose
This phase handles the highest security and privacy findings. The extension processes decrypted messages, SMS text, links, file URLs, device records, and credentials. Debug paths currently persist and render too much of that data.

## Audit Evidence
```ts
// src/background/index.ts
debugLogger.general("DEBUG", "FULL DECRYPTED PUSH DATA", {
  completeData: decryptedPush,
});
```

```ts
// src/debug-dashboard/index.ts
logsContainer.innerHTML = [...filteredLogs].reverse().map(log => {
  const dataStr = log.data ? JSON.stringify(log.data, null, 2) : '';
  return `<div class="log-message">${log.message}</div>${dataStr}`;
}).join('');
```

These paths combine into a concrete privacy/render issue: private user content can be persisted in logs and inserted into extension page markup.

## Design Direction
Use allowlist logging and DOM-safe rendering.

```ts
function summarizePushForLog(push: Push): Record<string, unknown> {
  return {
    iden: push.iden,
    type: push.type,
    encrypted: !!push.encrypted,
    hasBody: typeof push.body === 'string' && push.body.length > 0,
    hasUrl: typeof push.url === 'string' && push.url.length > 0,
  };
}
```

## Success Criteria
- Full decrypted pushes are never logged.
- SMS bodies, note bodies, URLs, file URLs, raw device data, API keys, tokens, and passwords are redacted or omitted.
- Debug dashboard cannot execute markup supplied through logs or errors.
- Tests include hostile strings like `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` and verify text rendering.

## File Scope
Primary file: `src/app/reconnect/index.ts`

Call sites to update:
- `src/background/utils.ts`
- `src/background/index.ts`

## Problem
`ensureConfigLoaded()` returns successfully without doing anything when called without setters/getters. Several wake-related paths call it without arguments and then read `getApiKey()`, believing storage hydration happened.

## Evidence
```ts
// src/app/reconnect/index.ts
export async function ensureConfigLoaded(stateSetters?, stateGetters?): Promise<void> {
  if (!stateSetters || !stateGetters) {
    // No state management provided, just return
    return;
  }

  const apiKey = await storageRepository.getApiKey();
  stateSetters.setApiKey(apiKey);
}
```

Known bad pattern:

```ts
// src/background/utils.ts
await ensureConfigLoaded();
const apiKey = getApiKey();
```

## Mitigation
Remove the no-arg API or make it real in a background-owned wrapper.

Preferred explicit adapter call:

```ts
await ensureConfigLoaded(
  { setApiKey, setDeviceIden, setAutoOpenLinks, setDeviceNickname, setNotificationTimeout },
  { getApiKey, getDeviceIden, getAutoOpenLinks, getDeviceNickname, getNotificationTimeout },
);
```

Alternative wrapper:

```ts
// src/background/config.ts
export async function hydrateBackgroundConfig(): Promise<void> {
  await ensureConfigLoaded(backgroundSetters, backgroundGetters);
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- `rg "ensureConfigLoaded\(\)" src` finds no silent no-op call sites, or each no-arg call invokes a real background hydrator.
- `SEND_PUSH` after service-worker wake can read the API key from storage.
- Health-check recovery reads storage before deciding recovery is impossible.

## Purpose
Fix the reliability root cause: after service-worker suspension or OS hibernate, the extension can wake with stale in-memory objects and a persisted `READY` state that no longer matches the actual WebSocket.

## Audit Evidence
Persisted `READY` is restored as if it were live operational truth:

```ts
// src/background/state-machine.ts
} else if (restoredState) {
  instance.currentState = restoredState;
  debugLogger.general("INFO", "[StateMachine] Hydrated state from storage", {
    restoredState: instance.currentState,
  });
}
```

Health check then detects a missing/disconnected socket but refuses to reconnect from `READY`:

```ts
// src/background/utils.ts
if (!websocketClient || !websocketClient.isConnected()) {
  const currentState = stateMachine.getCurrentState();

  if (currentState === ServiceWorkerState.IDLE) {
    stateMachine.transition("ATTEMPT_RECONNECT", { hasApiKey: true });
  } else if (currentState === ServiceWorkerState.DEGRADED || currentState === ServiceWorkerState.RECONNECTING) {
    connectFn();
  } else {
    debugLogger.websocket("DEBUG", "[HealthCheck] Skipping reconnect - unexpected state", { currentState });
  }
}
```

## Design Direction
Create one wake reconciliation path and call it from alarms, popup wake, manual reconnect, startup, and health check.

```ts
export async function reconcileWake(reason: string): Promise<void> {
  await hydrateBackgroundConfig();
  await stateMachineReady;
  ensureRecoveryAlarmsExist();

  const hasApiKey = !!getApiKey();
  const socketHealthy = !!websocketClient?.isConnected?.() && websocketClient.isConnectionHealthy();

  if (hasApiKey && !socketHealthy) {
    await stateMachine.transition('ATTEMPT_RECONNECT', {
      hasApiKey,
      socketHealthy,
      reason,
    });
  }
}
```

## Success Criteria
- `READY + null socket` reconnects.
- `READY + closed socket` reconnects.
- Reconnect decisions hydrate storage before reading `getApiKey()`.
- Permanent WebSocket close events use `WS_PERMANENT_ERROR`.
- Tests encode the hibernate-style stale `READY` state.

## Problem
When the host system hibernates and later resumes, the extension can wake with `lastKnownState = READY` but without a live WebSocket. The extension then displays or behaves as connected while real-time delivery is dead.

## Steps to Reproduce
1. Authenticate the extension and let it reach `READY`.
2. Hibernate or sleep the system long enough for the MV3 background service worker and socket to be gone.
3. Resume the system without restarting the browser.
4. Let an alarm fire or trigger manual wake.
5. Observe that the extension can remain on a stale `READY` path and fail to reconnect.

## Evidence
`READY` is restored as-is:

```ts
// src/background/state-machine.ts
} else if (restoredState) {
  instance.currentState = restoredState;
}
```

`READY` does not accept `ATTEMPT_RECONNECT`:

```ts
// src/background/state-machine.ts
case ServiceWorkerState.READY:
  if (event === 'WS_DISCONNECTED') return ServiceWorkerState.DEGRADED;
  if (event === 'WS_PERMANENT_ERROR') return ServiceWorkerState.ERROR;
  break;
```

Health check skips `READY + no socket`:

```ts
// src/background/utils.ts
if (!websocketClient || !websocketClient.isConnected()) {
  if (apiKey) {
    const currentState = stateMachine.getCurrentState();
    if (currentState === ServiceWorkerState.IDLE) {
      stateMachine.transition('ATTEMPT_RECONNECT', { hasApiKey: true });
    } else if (currentState === ServiceWorkerState.DEGRADED || currentState === ServiceWorkerState.RECONNECTING) {
      connectFn();
    } else {
      // READY lands here and no recovery happens.
    }
  }
}
```

## Mitigation
Treat persisted `READY` as UI history, not proof of a live socket. On wake, evaluate real credentials and socket health.

```ts
case ServiceWorkerState.READY:
  if (event === 'ATTEMPT_RECONNECT' && data?.hasApiKey && data?.socketHealthy === false) {
    return ServiceWorkerState.RECONNECTING;
  }
  if (event === 'WS_DISCONNECTED') return ServiceWorkerState.DEGRADED;
  if (event === 'WS_PERMANENT_ERROR') return ServiceWorkerState.ERROR;
  break;
```

The higher-value fix is a central reconciler:

```ts
await hydrateBackgroundConfig();
const socketHealthy = websocketClient?.isConnected?.() && websocketClient.isConnectionHealthy();
if (getApiKey() && !socketHealthy) {
  await stateMachine.transition('ATTEMPT_RECONNECT', { hasApiKey: true, socketHealthy: false });
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- Hibernate/resume with saved credentials reconnects without opening the popup.
- `READY + missing socket` triggers reconnect.
- `READY + unhealthy socket` triggers reconnect.
- `longSleepRecovery`, `websocketHealthCheck`, popup wake, and manual `attemptReconnect` call the same reconciliation function.
- Tests cover persisted `READY`, no live socket, and API key present in storage.

# B1 - Merge-preserve received SMS/mirror ephemerals (stop overwriting recentPushes)

Primary file: `src/app/session/index.ts` (+ small helper)

## Problem
Received SMS/mirror ephemerals are unshifted into `sessionCache.recentPushes` and saved, but the next display refresh replaces `recentPushes` wholesale with `/v2/pushes` results (which never contain ephemerals), wiping SMS from memory AND IndexedDB. SMS therefore vanishes from the popup on the next popup-open/refresh.

## Evidence
- Real-time write: `src/background/index.ts:491-494` (`unshift` + `saveSessionCache`).
- Overwrites: `src/app/session/index.ts:483` (init) and `:143` (`refreshSessionInBackground`): `sessionCache.recentPushes = displayPushes;`.
- Popup renders from `recentPushes`: `src/popup/index.ts:588-625,644-664`.

## Fix
Merge fresh `/v2/pushes` with previously-received ephemerals. Ephemerals usually lack a stable `iden`, so key by `type|created|body`; keep newest-first and capped:
```ts
// src/app/session/index.ts
function mergeKeepingEphemerals(fresh: Push[], prev: Push[]): Push[] {
  const isEphemeral = (p: Push) => p.type === "sms_changed" || p.type === "mirror";
  const key = (p: Push) =>
    p.iden ?? `${p.type}|${p.created ?? 0}|${"body" in p ? (p as { body?: string }).body ?? "" : ""}`;
  const keptEphemerals = (prev ?? []).filter(isEphemeral);
  const freshKeys = new Set(fresh.map(key));
  const merged = [...fresh, ...keptEphemerals.filter((p) => !freshKeys.has(key(p)))];
  return merged.sort((a, b) => (b.created || 0) - (a.created || 0)).slice(0, 200);
}
```
Apply at both overwrite sites:
```ts
// session/index.ts:483 and :143
sessionCache.recentPushes = mergeKeepingEphemerals(displayPushes, sessionCache.recentPushes);
```
Add an age cap (e.g., keep ephemerals from the last 24h) to prevent stale buildup.

## Acceptance criteria
- A received `sms_changed`/SMS `mirror` push remains in `recentPushes` after a subsequent `fetchDisplayPushes`-driven refresh AND after reload from IndexedDB.
- Regular `/v2/pushes` (note/link/file) behavior is unchanged; list remains capped and sorted newest-first.

## Verification
`npx vitest run tests/app tests/background`; add a test that seeds an SMS ephemeral, runs a display refresh, and asserts the SMS survives.

## Scope / parallelization
Independent; blocks B4. Coordinate with B3 (durable thread history) so the two display sources do not duplicate entries.

# A4 - WebSocket nop-timeout watchdog: self-close dead sockets

Primary file: `src/app/ws/client.ts`. Depends on A1.

## Problem
Dead-socket detection relies on `onclose`, which may not fire after OS resume (half-open). The client already tracks `lastNopAt` but never acts on staleness itself; only the external 1-/5-minute alarms do. Add an internal watchdog so that when no server `nop` arrives within the window, the client closes the socket and emits `websocket:disconnected`, letting the (A1-fixed) reconnect path run promptly.

## Evidence
- `src/app/ws/client.ts:35` `NOP_TIMEOUT = 60000`; `:152,192` `lastNopAt` set on open and on `nop`; `:363-368` `isConnectionHealthy`; `:270-310` `onclose` is the only disconnect trigger today.

## Fix
```ts
private nopTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null = null;

private armNopWatchdog(): void {
  if (this.nopTimer) clearTimeout(this.nopTimer);
  this.nopTimer = setTimeout(() => {
    if (!this.isConnectionHealthy()) {
      debugLogger.websocket("WARN", "No server nop within window - forcing reconnect", {
        ageMs: Date.now() - this.lastNopAt,
      });
      try { this.socket?.close(4999, "nop-timeout"); } catch { /* noop */ }
      globalEventBus.emit("websocket:disconnected", { code: 4999, reason: "nop-timeout" });
    }
  }, WebSocketClient.NOP_TIMEOUT + 5000); // small grace period
}
```
- Call `this.armNopWatchdog()` at the end of `onopen` and inside the `if (msg.type === "nop")` branch (right after updating `lastNopAt`).
- Clear it in `disconnect()`:
```ts
disconnect(): void {
  if (this.nopTimer) { clearTimeout(this.nopTimer); this.nopTimer = null; }
  if (this.socket) { /* existing close + null + stopMonitoring */ }
}
```
- IMPORTANT: code 4999 falls in the current permanent-close range (`code >= 4000 && code < 5000`) at `ws/client.ts:283-303`. Either emit `websocket:disconnected` directly (as above, bypassing `onclose` classification) or exclude the synthetic `nop-timeout` code from the permanent set so it is treated as recoverable.

## Acceptance criteria
- With no `nop` for longer than the window, the client emits `websocket:disconnected` without any external alarm, and (with A1) a fresh socket is created.
- A healthy stream (regular `nop`s) never triggers the watchdog.
- The watchdog timer is cleared on `disconnect()` (no leak across reconnects).

## Verification
`npx vitest run tests/app/ws-client.test.ts` with fake timers advanced past the window.

## Scope / parallelization
Blocked by A1. Self-contained in `WebSocketClient`.

# A3 - Re-arm recovery alarms at startup and on wake

Primary files: `src/background/index.ts`, `src/background/lifecycle.ts`, `src/app/session/index.ts`

## Problem
The 1-minute `websocketHealthCheck` alarm is created only inside `initializeSessionCache` (full network init). On a cache-hydrate startup, or after a browser restart that uses cache, that alarm may never be (re)created during the current service-worker generation, leaving only the 5-minute `longSleepRecovery` for recovery. Alarms should be idempotently ensured at every wake entry point.

## Evidence
- `src/app/session/index.ts:519` — `chrome.alarms.create("websocketHealthCheck", { periodInMinutes: 1 })` inside init only.
- `src/background/index.ts:1719-1730` — `onStartup`/`onInstalled` only call `ensureLongSleepRecoveryAlarm()`.

## Fix
Add one idempotent ensurer and call it from `onStartup`, `onInstalled`, and `reconcileWake`:
```ts
// src/background/index.ts
async function ensureRecoveryAlarmsExist(): Promise<void> {
  const have = new Set((await chrome.alarms.getAll()).map((a) => a.name));
  if (!have.has("longSleepRecovery"))    chrome.alarms.create("longSleepRecovery",    { periodInMinutes: 5 });
  if (!have.has("websocketHealthCheck")) chrome.alarms.create("websocketHealthCheck", { periodInMinutes: 1 });
}

chrome.runtime.onStartup.addListener(async () => {
  await ensureDebugConfigLoadedOnce();
  await ensureRecoveryAlarmsExist();   // replaces ensureLongSleepRecoveryAlarm()
  void bootstrap("startup");
  setTimeout(checkExtensionHealth, 5000);
});
chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(async () => {
  await ensureDebugConfigLoadedOnce();
  await ensureRecoveryAlarmsExist();
  void bootstrap("install");
});
```
Wire it into `reconcileWake` via dependency injection (lifecycle.ts already receives a deps object — avoids a circular import):
```ts
// src/background/lifecycle.ts (LifecycleCoordinatorDeps gains ensureRecoveryAlarms)
async function reconcileWake(reason: string): Promise<void> {
  await deps.hydrateConfig();
  await deps.stateMachineReady;
  await deps.ensureRecoveryAlarms();
  // ...existing apiKey/socketHealthy logic unchanged...
}
```

## Acceptance criteria
- After a cache-hydrate startup (no full init), both `websocketHealthCheck` and `longSleepRecovery` exist (assert via a `chrome.alarms.getAll` mock).
- Calling `reconcileWake` re-creates a missing health-check alarm.

## Verification
`npx vitest run tests/background/session-cache.test.ts tests/background`; `npm run typecheck`.

