## Problem
WebSocket errors only log. Permanent closes notify the user but do not send the state machine through `WS_PERMANENT_ERROR`.

## Evidence
```ts
// src/app/ws/client.ts
this.socket.onerror = (error) => {
  debugLogger.websocket("ERROR", "WebSocket error occurred", errorInfo);
  globalErrorTracker.trackError(websocketError, {...}, "WEBSOCKET");
};
```

```ts
// src/app/ws/client.ts
this.socket.onclose = (event) => {
  globalEventBus.emit("websocket:disconnected", closeInfo);

  if (event.code === 1008 || event.code === 4001 || (event.code >= 4000 && event.code < 5000)) {
    showPermanentWebSocketError(closeInfo);
    return;
  }
};
```

## Mitigation
Classify before emitting the lifecycle event.

```ts
const permanent =
  event.code === 1008 ||
  event.code === 4001 ||
  (event.code >= 4000 && event.code < 5000);

if (permanent) {
  globalEventBus.emit('websocket:permanent-error', closeInfo);
  globalEventBus.emit('websocket:state', 'permanent-error');
  showPermanentWebSocketError(closeInfo);
  return;
}

globalEventBus.emit('websocket:disconnected', closeInfo);
```

Then wire background:

```ts
globalEventBus.on('websocket:permanent-error', async () => {
  await stateMachineReady;
  await stateMachine.transition('WS_PERMANENT_ERROR');
});
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- Close code `1008` transitions to `ERROR`.
- Close code `4001` and other `4xxx` app codes transition to `ERROR`.
- Non-permanent close transitions through degraded/reconnect behavior.
- Tests assert event ordering.

# B3 - Fetch SMS thread history via /v2/permanents and resolve sms_changed

Primary file: `src/app/api/client.ts` (+ integration in `src/background/index.ts`, optional popup history). Single task leaf (per decision). Blocks B4.

## Problem
SMS is only ever seen as transient real-time ephemerals; there is no history fetch, and a `sms_changed` that carries no `notifications` body cannot be resolved to content. The proper Pushbullet mechanism is the SMS "permanents" store on the SMS-capable device.

## Evidence
- No `/v2/permanents` anywhere; API client only hits `/v2/pushes`, `/v2/devices`, `/v2/users/me`, `/v2/chats`, `/v2/upload-request` (`src/app/api/client.ts`).
- Empty `sms_changed` is dropped with no fallback (`src/background/utils.ts:409-416`).
- Device capability exists but is unused for gating: `Device.has_sms` (`src/types/domain.ts:32`).

## Fix (skeleton)
Add thread + thread-detail fetchers. The SMS device iden is the phone's, found via `has_sms`:
```ts
// src/app/api/client.ts
const PERMANENTS_URL = `${API_BASE_URL}/permanents`;

export interface SmsThread { id: string; recipients?: Array<{ name?: string; address?: string }>; latest?: { body?: string; timestamp?: number }; }
export interface SmsMessage { id: string; type: "incoming" | "outgoing"; body?: string; timestamp?: number; image_url?: string; }

export async function fetchSmsThreads(apiKey: string, deviceIden: string): Promise<SmsThread[]> {
  const res = await fetch(`${PERMANENTS_URL}/${deviceIden}_threads`, { headers: authHeaders(apiKey) });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to fetch SMS threads: ${res.status}`);
  const data = await res.json();                 // confirm exact shape against live data
  return data?.data?.threads ?? data?.threads ?? [];
}

export async function fetchSmsThread(apiKey: string, deviceIden: string, threadId: string): Promise<SmsMessage[]> {
  const res = await fetch(`${PERMANENTS_URL}/${deviceIden}_thread_${threadId}`, { headers: authHeaders(apiKey) });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to fetch SMS thread ${threadId}: ${res.status}`);
  const data = await res.json();
  return data?.data?.thread ?? data?.thread ?? [];
}
```
Integration on a `sms_changed` ephemeral (background): pick the SMS device and, when the ephemeral lacks a usable body, fetch the latest thread to populate the notification and seed durable popup history:
```ts
const smsDevice = sessionCache.devices.find((d) => d.has_sms);
if (smsDevice) {
  const threads = await fetchSmsThreads(apiKey, smsDevice.iden);
  // newest thread -> latest message -> title/body for the notification + recentPushes/history
}
```
Notes:
- Permanents payloads may be E2EE-encrypted too — reuse the B2 password path before parsing.
- Cache threads in `sessionCache` (new field) and persist, so the popup can show recent conversations across restarts (this is what makes SMS "display" durably). Respect the existing 200-item cap or use a dedicated SMS list.
- VERIFY the exact Pushbullet response shapes against live data during implementation (the `data.*` wrappers above are the common shape but must be confirmed).

## Acceptance criteria
- On a `sms_changed` tickle, the extension fetches the SMS device's latest thread and shows the message even when the ephemeral body is empty.
- The popup shows recent SMS threads/messages after a service-worker restart (served from persisted cache, not just live ephemerals).
- Encrypted permanents are handled via the configured password; an absent password reuses the B2 prompt.

## Verification
`npx vitest run tests/app/api-client.test.ts tests/background` with mocked `/v2/permanents` responses (including empty and encrypted); manual end-to-end with a real phone.

## Scope / parallelization
Largest leaf; blocks B4. Independent of Phase A. Keep behind `has_sms` detection so accounts without an SMS device do no extra network work.

# B2 - Surface encrypted SMS instead of silently dropping it

Primary file: `src/background/index.ts` (`websocket:push` handler)

## Problem
When an ephemeral is end-to-end encrypted and no password is configured (common for Pushbullet SMS mirroring), the handler logs a WARN and returns — the user sees nothing and has no idea SMS is being suppressed.

## Evidence
- `src/background/index.ts:382-438`: decrypt attempt; `:407-413` "no encryption password set" -> `decryptionFailed`; `:427-438` early `return`.

## Fix
Show a single actionable notification when decryption is impossible due to a missing password, then return:
```ts
if (decryptionFailed) {
  const hasPwd = !!(await storageRepository.getEncryptionPassword());
  if (!hasPwd) {
    // stable id => repeated drops do not spam the user
    await createNotificationWithTimeout(
      "pushbullet-need-e2e-password",
      {
        type: "basic",
        iconUrl: chrome.runtime.getURL("icons/icon128.png"),
        title: "Encrypted message received",
        message: "Set your Pushbullet end-to-end password in Options to view encrypted SMS/notifications.",
        priority: 2,
      },
      undefined,
      0, // no auto-dismiss
    );
  }
  debugLogger.general("WARN", "Encrypted ephemeral dropped", { hasPwd });
  return;
}
```
Optionally route a click on this notification to `chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage()`.

## Acceptance criteria
- E2EE on + no password => exactly one actionable prompt (not one per message); a password present => SMS decrypts and displays unchanged.
- No regression for unencrypted ephemerals.

## Verification
`npx vitest run tests/background`; mock `getEncryptionPassword` to null and assert the prompt path; mock a password and assert the decrypt path still runs.

## Scope / parallelization
Independent; complements B3 (permanents may also be encrypted and use the same password).

# A2 - chrome.idle wake detection -> reconcileWake on resume

Primary files: `manifest.json`, `src/background/index.ts`

## Problem
There is no proactive wake trigger. After long sleep, recovery waits for the next alarm, which Chrome may coalesce/delay (ADR-0007 acknowledges this). `chrome.idle` fires promptly when the user returns from idle/locked and is a strong proxy for machine wake.

## Evidence
- `manifest.json:19-25` permissions: storage, notifications, contextMenus, tabs, alarms — no `idle`.
- No `chrome.idle` usage in src (verified by search).

## Fix
manifest.json:
```json
"permissions": ["storage", "notifications", "contextMenus", "tabs", "alarms", "idle"],
```
src/background/index.ts (`reconcileWake` is already in scope from `createLifecycleCoordinator`):
```ts
try {
  chrome.idle.setDetectionInterval(60); // seconds
  chrome.idle.onStateChanged.addListener((state) => {
    if (state === "active") {
      debugLogger.general("INFO", "[Idle] Returned to active - reconciling wake");
      void reconcileWake("idle-active");
    }
  });
} catch (e) {
  debugLogger.general("WARN", "chrome.idle unavailable", { error: String(e) });
}
```

## Acceptance criteria
- Manifest declares `idle`. A simulated `onStateChanged('active')` calls `reconcileWake` exactly once; `locked`/`idle` states do not reconnect.
- The new permission is called out in release notes (Chrome re-prompts users to accept permissions on update).

## Verification
`npm run typecheck`; unit-test the listener; manual: lock/unlock or sleep/resume and confirm reconnect in logs.

## Scope / parallelization
Independent of A1/A3/A4. Bump patch version in package.json, manifest.json, options.html per repo policy (or defer to the end-of-tree bump).

